<div class="callout">
  <h2>Should You Upgrade?</h2>
  <p>If you don't already own a Thermomix®️, this isn't really a choice—the TM7 is the current generation sold new in Canada, so you're getting the latest model.</p>
  <p>If you already own a TM6, though, I think the decision is a little more personal.</p>
  <p>For me, the larger 10-inch screen is one of the biggest improvements. It's easier to see the recipe, follow the guided steps, and navigate Cookidoo while I'm cooking. I also really like being able to find a recipe on my phone and send it directly to my TM7 with Recipe Handover. The TM6 could sync with Cookidoo and access recipes from your phone, but the TM7 makes that handoff feel much more seamless.</p>
  <p>The other improvement I didn't expect to appreciate as much as I do is the insulated mixing bowl. It's more comfortable and reassuring to handle, especially when my 11-year-old is helping in the kitchen. I feel much more at ease letting her handle the bowl because the insulation helps keep the outside cooler. And that insulation also contributes to one of the TM7's most noticeable improvements: it's dramatically quieter. Vorwerk measures the TM7 at about 35 dB at soft speed/speed 1, compared with about 63 dB for the TM6 under the same test conditions.</p>
  <p>So, would I upgrade?</p>
  <p>If you cook regularly and appreciate a better, quieter, more family-friendly experience, I think the TM7 is a meaningful upgrade. The bigger screen, easier recipe handoff, insulated bowl, and quieter operation are improvements you'll notice every day.</p>
  <p>If you already have a TM6 that works perfectly and you only cook with it occasionally, I'd be less inclined to rush out and upgrade. The TM6 still has access to Cookidoo's recipe ecosystem, and you aren't suddenly missing out on the thousands of recipes available to Thermomix owners.</p>
  <p>For me, though, the TM7 isn't just about having the newest model. It's about making the machine easier and more comfortable for my whole family to use—and that's something I notice every time we cook together.</p>
</div>

